### create a room to update (run first, then replace :id below with the returned id) -> 201
POST http://localhost:3000/rooms/new HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": "update target",
	"visibility": "public",
	"description": "before update"
}

### owner updates their own room -> 200
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": "updated name",
	"description": "after update"
}

### partial update — only description changes, name stays untouched -> 200
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"description": "only the description changes this time"
}

### non-owner tries to update -> 403 Forbidden (user 2 doesn't own the room created above)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 2

{
	"name": "hijacked"
}

### update a room that doesn't exist -> 404 Not Found
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/999999 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": "ghost room"
}

### missing x-user-id header -> 401 Unauthorized
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"name": "no auth"
}

### x-user-id with no matching user in DB -> 401 Unauthorized
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 999999

{
	"name": "ghost user"
}

### empty name -> 400 Bad Request (zod min(1) still enforced on the partial schema)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": ""
}

### invalid visibility value -> 400 Bad Request (zod enum mismatch)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"visibility": "secret"
}

### non-integer room id -> 400 Bad Request (ParseIntPipe)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/abc HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": "n/a"
}

### extra/unknown fields are stripped, not persisted -> 200, status/createdById stay as they were
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": "still just the owner",
	"status": "closed",
	"createdById": 999
}

### updating a closed room -> 403 Forbidden ("Poll is closed" message, service applies the Poll copy to Room)
### depends on seeded data: replace :id with a room whose status is "closed" from your seed
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": "should not apply"
}
